{:db/id 17592186115193 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id 17592186115022 :question/id #uuid "83b8a6dd-c8c4-5537-ac88-289265752755" :question/math-academy-id "e-3648" :question/problem "Find the slope of $y=f(x)$ at $x=\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}$ if $f(x) = \\dfrac{-2\\cot x}{\\sin x}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the derivative using the quotient rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{-2cot⁡x}{sin⁡x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-2cot⁡x)\\cdot sin⁡x-(-2cot⁡x)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(sin⁡x)}{{[sin⁡x]}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2(-{csc}^{2}⁡x)\\cdot sin⁡x+2cot⁡x\\cdot (cos⁡x)}{{sin}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{2csc⁡x+2cot⁡xcos⁡x}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $x=\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}$ in the derivative and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =\\frac{2csc⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})+2cot⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})cos⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})}{{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot (\\sqrt{2})+2\\cdot (1)\\cdot (\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})}{{(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{(\\frac{1}{2})} \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7995b377-1de4-5126-aa29-8cc30b4918f8" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id 17592186048465} {:db/id 17592186050711}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id 17592186115528 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2092ed7b-78ba-5b08-8ed9-5a3ae1c22f13" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{3})-\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\sqrt{3})\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\sqrt{3})-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id 17592186285080} {:answer/id #uuid "61025999-7cbd-5360-838b-eda24fb2a51c" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-11\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{3})-\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\sqrt{3})\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\sqrt{3})-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id 17592186285678} {:answer/id #uuid "a9b589e9-9125-5e9a-b153-823caacb3c8a" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-11\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{3})+\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\sqrt{3})\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\sqrt{3})+\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id 17592186286334} {:answer/id #uuid "b5151810-8b1c-5b10-a7e3-87a15f4d9958" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{3})-\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\sqrt{3})\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\sqrt{3})-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id 17592186286435} {:answer/id #uuid "daba25ff-6035-5619-8ac0-07d5eb9bd01a" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-11\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{3})-\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\sqrt{3})\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\sqrt{3})-1" :db/id 17592186286782}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "61025999-7cbd-5360-838b-eda24fb2a51c" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-11\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{3})-\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\sqrt{3})\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\sqrt{3})-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id 17592186285678} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab8dc92d-302f-5800-8e99-962388310e9e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186287498}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c56fab41-d998-532e-9118-40493f1a0626" :question/math-academy-id "q-1886" :question/problem "Find the slope of $y=f(x)$ at $x=\\sqrt{3}$ if $f(x)=11\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+\\frac{1}{x}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the derivative using the sum rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(11\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+\\frac{1}{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(11\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+{x}^{-1}) \\\\  & =11(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)-\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =-11\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $x=\\sqrt{3}$ in the derivative and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(\\sqrt{3}) & =-11\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{3})-\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\sqrt{3})\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\sqrt{3})-\\frac{1}{(\\sqrt{3})^{2}} \\\\  & =-11\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{3})-\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\sqrt{3})\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\sqrt{3})-\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186115531 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "83d05e6b-994a-5931-90fb-0244e740694f" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id 17592186285997} {:answer/id #uuid "b9702af1-9a01-5ff4-990f-2b8e8b2bf574" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6\\sqrt{2}+2" :db/id 17592186286475} {:answer/id #uuid "c916f7e2-e71d-5044-a1e6-83799fa5fc80" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}+2" :db/id 17592186286622} {:answer/id #uuid "e5017828-3ef7-5857-8b3a-d98ae9e0243d" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id 17592186286882} {:answer/id #uuid "e79e42be-aa4f-50c1-a571-518a34f7f2ac" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\sqrt{2}+2" :db/id 17592186286908}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e5017828-3ef7-5857-8b3a-d98ae9e0243d" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id 17592186286882} :answer-field/id #uuid "8379a3b1-8766-53c7-86da-7fc0c6df7e5d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186287424}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "18111828-8d82-5c70-b695-6858b89927bd" :question/math-academy-id "q-1905" :question/problem "Find the slope of $y=f(x)$ at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ if $f(x)=2x-\\sqrt{2}sec⁡x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the derivative using the sum rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2x-\\sqrt{2}sec⁡x) \\\\  & =2-\\sqrt{2}sec⁡xtan⁡x\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ in the derivative and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =2-\\sqrt{2}sec⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})tan⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =2-\\sqrt{2}(\\sqrt{2})(1) \\\\  & =2-2 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186233087 :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8cc9778d-34a0-53fe-a02e-327d24fefea1" :question/math-academy-id "q-104437" :question/problem "Find the slope of $y=f(x)$ at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ if $f(x)=x\\operatorname{cot}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we take the derivative using the product rule:\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x\\operatorname{cot}x) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cot}x+x(-{csc}^{2}x) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cot}x-x{csc}^{2}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ in the derivative and get\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{\\pi /4} & =\\operatorname{cot}(\\frac{\\pi }{4})-\\frac{\\pi }{4}{csc}^{2}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =1-\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\cdot (\\sqrt{2})^{2} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186233911 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03e9d963-612a-5223-a2bb-a0380a286d94" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id 17592186232832}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "03e9d963-612a-5223-a2bb-a0380a286d94" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id 17592186232832} :answer-field/id #uuid "56422a4a-1f7d-5745-b018-ef376ed6e05f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186232831}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6e21b5cf-a720-5e69-8578-f6d79190e60d" :question/math-academy-id "q-340642" :question/problem "Find the slope $m$ of $y=g(x)$ at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ if $g(x)=\\operatorname{csc}x\\operatorname{cot}x.$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the derivative using the product rule and sum rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{'}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{csc}x\\operatorname{cot}x) \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{csc}x\\operatorname{cot}x)(\\operatorname{cot}x)+(\\operatorname{csc}x)(-{csc}^{2}x) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{csc}x({cot}^{2}x+{csc}^{2}x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and evaluate the slope $m:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m={g}^{'}(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =-\\operatorname{csc}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})[{cot}^{2}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+{csc}^{2}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})] \\\\  & =-1\\cdot ({0}^{2}+{1}^{2}) \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186240879 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18f7e706-6667-560b-bd84-79164bd2ed56" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id 17592186238265} {:answer/id #uuid "485520fe-f7db-5462-90b3-8b9dc00969d6" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id 17592186238684} {:answer/id #uuid "4ebd5941-c9bf-5355-a88c-6736db31de31" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id 17592186238730} {:answer/id #uuid "746fc071-c68b-5025-87be-eb8a9b327237" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id 17592186239055} {:answer/id #uuid "fe35b390-cf3c-53c9-b56a-b8e3bb467faa" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id 17592186240302}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "746fc071-c68b-5025-87be-eb8a9b327237" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id 17592186239055} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a5d153b-a4b3-593f-9ec7-5127df5989a0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186240372}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "10b5a865-9dfd-5753-8931-5381fe6e32af" :question/math-academy-id "q-104442" :question/problem "Find the slope of $y=f(x)$ at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ if $f(x)=\\frac{sec⁡x}{\\sqrt{3}}+\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{\\pi }.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we take the derivative of each term and then add them, as follows:\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{sec⁡x}{\\sqrt{3}}+\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{\\pi }) \\\\  & =\\frac{sec⁡xtan⁡x}{\\sqrt{3}}+\\frac{6x}{\\pi }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $x=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ in the derivative and get\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{\\pi /3} & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\cdot sec⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\cdot tan⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})+\\frac{6}{\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\cdot 2\\cdot \\sqrt{3}+2 \\\\  & =2+2 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186287917 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04d15acc-1672-5ec4-bb78-f3474884b897" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{3}-5\\sqrt{3}" :db/id 17592186284830} {:answer/id #uuid "48fabaf5-be8a-589c-8cf0-074c455a9240" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}-10\\sqrt{3}" :db/id 17592186285458} {:answer/id #uuid "63f73e2e-4004-5fc8-9825-f8337f6c2b07" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{6}-10\\sqrt{3}" :db/id 17592186285697} {:answer/id #uuid "766bb2aa-4af5-5e09-aed3-a777505c1a5c" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}+10\\sqrt{3}" :db/id 17592186285891} {:answer/id #uuid "e40e7c86-1ed2-5d5e-9940-61e65ceaec5c" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{3}-10\\sqrt{3}" :db/id 17592186286873}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e40e7c86-1ed2-5d5e-9940-61e65ceaec5c" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{3}-10\\sqrt{3}" :db/id 17592186286873} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8570317-ecab-5ed9-a868-188d2c2ead8e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186287627}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f9daa906-697e-5ad9-9a96-96e98679f403" :question/math-academy-id "q-1904" :question/problem "Find the slope of $y=f(x)$ at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ if $f(x)=-{x}^{2}+5csc⁡x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the derivative using the sum rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{d}{dx}(-{x}^{2}+5csc⁡x) \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-x)+5(-csc⁡xcot⁡x) \\\\  & =-2x-5csc⁡xcot⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ into the derivative and get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) & =-2(\\frac{\\pi }{6})-5csc⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})cot⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{3}-5\\cdot 2\\cdot \\sqrt{3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{3}-10\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186314986 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4212e2b2-4307-5ba7-9307-27d580b7ec58" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{\\pi }" :db/id 17592186312499}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4212e2b2-4307-5ba7-9307-27d580b7ec58" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{\\pi }" :db/id 17592186312499} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f109190-b06a-563b-a599-ac63006fd39c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186314275}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a443ce48-9d5c-5ad3-838c-31eadde39a66" :question/math-academy-id "q-340630" :question/problem "Find the slope $m$ of $y=h(x)$ at $x=\\pi $ if $h(x)={e}^{x}+3\\operatorname{sec}⁡x.$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x}+3\\operatorname{sec}⁡x) \\\\  & ={e}^{x}+3\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $x=\\pi $ and evaluate the slope $m:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m={h}^{′}(\\pi ) & ={e}^{\\pi }+3\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\pi )\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\pi ) \\\\  & ={e}^{\\pi }+3\\cdot (-1)\\cdot 0 \\\\  & ={e}^{\\pi }\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186314990 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "faba1883-af56-500b-a141-28392efb394f" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id 17592186313976}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "faba1883-af56-500b-a141-28392efb394f" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id 17592186313976} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f7953c8-2aeb-585d-85e3-e06ca80b78e1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186314349}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "19b497f4-a444-5fb7-80fe-a52cd36cf318" :question/math-academy-id "q-340660" :question/problem "Find the slope of $y=f(x)$ at $x=0$ if $f(x)=\\frac{4x}{sec⁡x}.$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the derivative using the quotient rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{4x}{sec⁡x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4x)\\cdot sec⁡x-4x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(sec⁡x)}{{sec}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{4sec⁡x-4x\\cdot sec⁡xtan⁡x}{{sec}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{4sec⁡x(1-xtan⁡x)}{{sec}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{4(1-xtan⁡x)}{sec⁡x}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $x=0$ in the derivative and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(0) & =\\frac{4(1-0\\cdot tan⁡0)}{sec⁡0} \\\\  & =\\frac{4(1-0)}{1} \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186338841 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20324c7d-2431-5dbf-89ba-4a62fbbbbdeb" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-\\frac{3}{\\pi }" :db/id 17592186336333} {:answer/id #uuid "2d601842-f51f-5a34-901c-3c87ed74673e" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{\\pi }-2" :db/id 17592186336467} {:answer/id #uuid "c6ecc1e0-b453-5588-a3e8-923b6e7ebcab" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi -2" :db/id 17592186337797} {:answer/id #uuid "ec9d4934-d293-54d1-9eb4-aaf1a8bf5781" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{\\pi }" :db/id 17592186338096} {:answer/id #uuid "ef4a666c-1131-5d8c-a6c2-62062090c6e3" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{\\pi }+2" :db/id 17592186338125}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2d601842-f51f-5a34-901c-3c87ed74673e" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{\\pi }-2" :db/id 17592186336467} :answer-field/id #uuid "743b193f-17c2-5199-b0eb-adc69b1674c6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186338476}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b4b4054a-401d-511c-ba0c-65722b1ecab6" :question/math-academy-id "q-70874" :question/problem "Find the slope of $y=f(x)$ at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ if $f(x)=ln⁡x+3csc⁡x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the derivative using the sum rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ln⁡x+3csc⁡x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x}+3(-csc⁡xcot⁡x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x}-3csc⁡xcot⁡x\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $x=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ in the derivative and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) & =\\frac{1}{(\\frac{\\pi }{3})}-3csc⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})cot⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\pi }-3(\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}})(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\pi }-3(\\frac{2}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\pi }-2.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Slope of the Tangent at a Point of a Function Involving Reciprocal Trigonometric Functions"}
